  'Prepare elementary teacher candidates to design, teach, assess, and revise mathematics instruction that develops conceptual understanding, procedural fluency, reasoning, discourse, identity, and equitable access across K-6 classrooms.',
  $temajson${"slug": "teaching-elementary-mathematics", "title": "Teaching Elementary Mathematics", "description": "Prepare elementary teacher candidates to design, teach, assess, and revise mathematics instruction that develops conceptual understanding, procedural fluency, reasoning, discourse, identity, and equitable access across K-6 classrooms.", "topics": [{"id": "3d1830b3-293c-4cbe-be22-08212023f900", "type": "topic", "title": "Foundations of Elementary Mathematics Teaching and Mathematical Identity", "description": "Elementary mathematics teaching begins with a view of children as sense-makers. This topic frames math as reasoning, communication, representation, and productive struggle rather than memorized procedures alone.", "children": [{"id": "15bf01eb-9b35-429a-ab1b-0d88dc17663b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "What elementary math teaching is for", "children": [{"id": "8211297e-407d-4c05-8b2d-ac914c8cf872", "type": "concept", "title": "conceptual understanding"}, {"id": "1f51beb2-1a31-4bfd-aae6-3b8cffc6c942", "type": "concept", "title": "procedural fluency"}, {"id": "fe71b4d7-41f5-4945-a63a-570b77df7d25", "type": "concept", "title": "strategic competence"}, {"id": "9f1b791e-11cd-420f-a628-baeb472cd8cd", "type": "concept", "title": "productive disposition"}], "description": "Why it matters: Teachers learn to design experiences that build flexible thinking, confidence, and durable mathematical understanding."}, {"id": "9876e976-4a6a-4975-a4c6-ffebdb4bb034", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mathematical identity and agency", "children": [{"id": "c5f28279-eb46-4f6f-b55d-cffc0d7772c0", "type": "concept", "title": "growth mindset with evidence"}, {"id": "9609ccac-5e10-4bfe-8e87-fbdd573d5d4f", "type": "concept", "title": "belonging"}, {"id": "dfcfb82c-7ecc-4106-bddc-513e99d31c6e", "type": "concept", "title": "student voice"}, {"id": "eed639b9-c0f4-4161-9ca1-dd1048af559a", "type": "concept", "title": "teacher expectations"}], "description": "Why it matters: Students' beliefs about who can do mathematics shape participation and persistence, so identity work is instructional work."}, {"id": "5ed38188-e68a-459b-8c07-851eab6d01b0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Effective teaching practices", "children": [{"id": "61d78f16-6c8e-4033-a2b5-49b425f32d1a", "type": "concept", "title": "NCTM teaching practices"}, {"id": "f9d8024a-2f19-484e-a78b-1dfedf4f3373", "type": "concept", "title": "task launch"}, {"id": "5ae7f0ba-18e8-4003-a40a-8b61cf403637", "type": "concept", "title": "facilitation moves"}, {"id": "bb28de67-8038-4636-af71-0315af186d11", "type": "concept", "title": "reflection routines"}], "description": "Why it matters: Research-based practices give teachers a shared language for planning, launching, facilitating, and reflecting on math lessons."}]}, {"id": "bc3527e5-3ef9-4207-82c8-03d4482704ec", "type": "topic", "title": "Learning Progressions, Standards, and Curriculum Coherence", "description": "This section connects grade-level teaching to the larger developmental arc of K-6 mathematics. Teachers learn to see how today's lesson depends on prior ideas and prepares students for future ones.", "children": [{"id": "5de33baf-7c7f-491c-b3f1-9780dabc5817", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Standards and progressions", "children": [{"id": "95bf79c5-78d7-443e-9a43-e6e3d9f04fb9", "type": "concept", "title": "Common Core domains"}, {"id": "a0ad641c-43d5-4d0d-b600-5b81139d21c0", "type": "concept", "title": "NCTM process standards"}, {"id": "4e45bbe4-000e-4cdd-a41a-e546f2e08465", "type": "concept", "title": "vertical alignment"}, {"id": "69814ae1-1839-48f0-97f2-3ec535652990", "type": "concept", "title": "prerequisite knowledge"}], "description": "Why it matters: Standards become useful when teachers understand the learning trajectory behind them, not just the grade-level checklist."}, {"id": "6fcac5b9-18a4-4b68-8b7f-8c37b5f74ea0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Curriculum analysis", "children": [{"id": "e85b575a-b779-4f68-8173-2126d40d8970", "type": "concept", "title": "scope and sequence"}, {"id": "56fa63ad-bf84-47bc-aa1a-04fd0c14ab20", "type": "concept", "title": "lesson purpose"}, {"id": "328bd41a-bc4e-4e75-ac64-7cb997b4898d", "type": "concept", "title": "task quality"}, {"id": "ad7b63db-eb37-49d2-8d23-cc8716d61f21", "type": "concept", "title": "adaptation decisions"}], "description": "Why it matters: Teachers evaluate materials for coherence, cognitive demand, representation, and equity rather than simply following pages."}, {"id": "b4803087-1114-4d71-b345-21e9c126b0e8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Backward design", "children": [{"id": "f5bc7754-7af6-480f-aa47-5e8b7867f7ec", "type": "concept", "title": "learning goals"}, {"id": "841679fc-9d3c-4d85-9eb4-de31f8381e1e", "type": "concept", "title": "success criteria"}, {"id": "213d7e99-ccec-4796-86a4-cb2b23c98d19", "type": "concept", "title": "assessment evidence"}, {"id": "7433d321-b0ba-4ef5-8754-ecf51309784c", "type": "concept", "title": "lesson arcs"}], "description": "Why it matters: Planning starts from evidence of understanding, then selects tasks, questions, and supports that make that understanding visible."}]}, {"id": "0bba44b2-7bed-4cc1-acab-37b8f8ec49d4", "type": "topic", "title": "Number Sense, Counting, Place Value, and Base-Ten Reasoning", "description": "Number sense is the foundation for nearly every elementary math idea. This topic develops children's ability to count, compare, compose, decompose, estimate, and reason with our base-ten system.", "children": [{"id": "ea2e32ad-f701-4889-b1f0-d87238592a63", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Counting and cardinality", "children": [{"id": "a9a1cb07-844a-4140-95ef-aa6825cede96", "type": "concept", "title": "one-to-one correspondence"}, {"id": "d759b460-da9a-4c76-8363-7214b690e01d", "type": "concept", "title": "stable order"}, {"id": "04f2ea9c-bfd8-4536-8bea-bb7a774dedf1", "type": "concept", "title": "cardinality"}, {"id": "e59f0ece-3a6f-4fcf-902c-0b0ae114cfae", "type": "concept", "title": "subitizing"}], "description": "Why it matters: Counting is a conceptual system that links number words, objects, order, quantity, and comparison."}, {"id": "6cb23fcb-acf0-4535-b419-1d2e05515a49", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Place value", "children": [{"id": "af60de93-46ff-47b4-a869-97833a1632fa", "type": "concept", "title": "unitizing"}, {"id": "61b4dd2a-e9fe-4c54-b44a-5a2b935c9dfd", "type": "concept", "title": "bundling"}, {"id": "76b9e054-f5d5-452c-a3fd-7f0c5ea7fd1e", "type": "concept", "title": "expanded form"}, {"id": "ec4cedbe-804c-4fa4-9496-1f002cbc2766", "type": "concept", "title": "base-ten blocks"}], "description": "Why it matters: Place value helps students treat numbers as structured quantities, making later computation and estimation meaningful."}, {"id": "328f6b60-fdde-4a0f-b7b9-23925c7e9225", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Estimation and mental math", "children": [{"id": "e9ea507e-0894-4454-b195-5f148a459608", "type": "concept", "title": "benchmark numbers"}, {"id": "ba0df21b-de05-48e8-9f13-15b847af16fb", "type": "concept", "title": "rounding"}, {"id": "a27b7e10-6e72-4048-8f48-2a84b2562980", "type": "concept", "title": "compensation"}, {"id": "26c8ff90-2cde-408b-ac1c-fecb6a084919", "type": "concept", "title": "number lines"}], "description": "Why it matters: Estimation builds reasonableness and flexible strategy use instead of answer-only habits."}]}, {"id": "e0060e30-3c81-4b48-978d-f545d7e743f1", "type": "topic", "title": "Addition, Subtraction, Multiplication, and Division Concepts", "description": "Operations become powerful when children understand the situations, relationships, and representations behind them. This topic moves from problem structures to strategies and fluency.", "children": [{"id": "52860d6f-c6e9-4164-af92-cdbbce34e1a5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Additive reasoning", "children": [{"id": "a2cb3d86-7e73-4292-a9a9-c8592e298666", "type": "concept", "title": "part-part-whole"}, {"id": "f1745a12-76d0-46de-b23b-681a251d7f8e", "type": "concept", "title": "comparison problems"}, {"id": "8df59146-b0b6-4f4f-87fa-ac749a6e38be", "type": "concept", "title": "unknown positions"}, {"id": "cc00a3ec-603c-4782-b5b7-b4f1bc6a563f", "type": "concept", "title": "fact strategies"}], "description": "Why it matters: Addition and subtraction are related operations used to join, separate, compare, and find unknowns."}, {"id": "764c594a-fced-4422-8f62-3631772f7056", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multiplicative reasoning", "children": [{"id": "d5950672-cb77-41ca-9c93-deb419247f0a", "type": "concept", "title": "equal groups"}, {"id": "b7e8466c-a44f-4b0d-8a59-61225e9c71ee", "type": "concept", "title": "arrays"}, {"id": "45cb3eb0-22bf-4dec-a5b0-4e5fbf31d2be", "type": "concept", "title": "area model"}, {"id": "c62a0dfc-a6c1-421d-a702-f56f750ba00c", "type": "concept", "title": "measurement division"}, {"id": "84a3fd4d-2a8b-460e-98af-10ff93c45ca8", "type": "concept", "title": "partitive division"}], "description": "Why it matters: Multiplication and division extend counting into equal groups, arrays, rates, and comparisons."}, {"id": "ec9e0b49-8217-48e3-9ec7-08488abb4ca8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fluency development", "children": [{"id": "90e00f3e-d2a7-4e8e-91f7-5eb853d7a90c", "type": "concept", "title": "derived facts"}, {"id": "80b2c536-24f0-42e7-a3dc-3f4ff07553b2", "type": "concept", "title": "strategy interviews"}, {"id": "b055b323-615f-4768-962d-71823610a65c", "type": "concept", "title": "games"}, {"id": "962735f9-0466-4f8d-9796-e3b866217229", "type": "concept", "title": "practice design"}], "description": "Why it matters: Fluency means accuracy, efficiency, flexibility, and understanding, not timed recall alone."}]}, {"id": "328ea6d4-18ce-4a12-9914-2c03ec555b4f", "type": "topic", "title": "Fractions, Decimals, Ratios, and Percent", "description": "Rational number concepts are a major transition in elementary mathematics. Teachers learn to help students coordinate units, equivalence, magnitude, and operations across multiple representations.", "children": [{"id": "c46e2988-ace8-4eee-92c5-5506d992bc87", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fractions as numbers", "children": [{"id": "cb9a9c09-cff6-4592-9e53-7b90e4b3791e", "type": "concept", "title": "unit fractions"}, {"id": "dcb3db99-8222-4acc-a648-3efaf16ed3e5", "type": "concept", "title": "iteration"}, {"id": "51270e41-ca9a-47d4-ac3a-5184f5a81d16", "type": "concept", "title": "partitioning"}, {"id": "19223cf0-fc1f-4960-872d-39b4367063d0", "type": "concept", "title": "benchmark fractions"}], "description": "Why it matters: Students need to see fractions as quantities on a number line, not only shaded parts of shapes."}, {"id": "0031624e-1e9b-47a7-b62c-f67294481598", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equivalence and comparison", "children": [{"id": "2cc89ff5-295c-4275-9807-fb7d8dbd1c42", "type": "concept", "title": "common units"}, {"id": "7d023d2c-bb1d-4ee4-8a2e-fc10a1c0ef8f", "type": "concept", "title": "equivalent fractions"}, {"id": "bb22a81a-5d10-4850-a1c8-c8271c1afbe1", "type": "concept", "title": "common denominators"}, {"id": "b0cf8307-b052-4ddd-a842-b9d8e697ba33", "type": "concept", "title": "cross-multiplication as reasoning"}], "description": "Why it matters: Equivalence links visual, numerical, and relational reasoning and prepares students for operations."}, {"id": "25ef6189-3b56-4227-9a6c-7029fe64e0ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Decimals, ratios, and percent", "children": [{"id": "18a4aecb-7d3c-4e26-89ea-b7999a9fa476", "type": "concept", "title": "decimal place value"}, {"id": "d071053e-ae47-4cbd-a010-be6b2c0a506c", "type": "concept", "title": "hundred grids"}, {"id": "1fefc910-09ad-4e7e-9ea3-130a78417a2b", "type": "concept", "title": "ratio tables"}, {"id": "e5368585-44d8-4db2-b3e7-3aa153ec1a89", "type": "concept", "title": "percent benchmarks"}], "description": "Why it matters: Decimals and percents extend base-ten and fraction reasoning into measurement, money, data, and proportional situations."}]}, {"id": "fcd67133-c1bb-4906-b2a9-fe5e95b46f23", "type": "topic", "title": "Geometry, Spatial Reasoning, Measurement, and Data", "description": "Geometry, measurement, and data connect mathematics to space, attributes, and evidence. Students learn to classify, measure, visualize, represent, and interpret the world quantitatively.", "children": [{"id": "d6d9f398-ae81-4ee4-80d2-a1239647a502", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Geometry and spatial visualization", "children": [{"id": "d725cf60-a8d0-435d-811d-52fe40e5158d", "type": "concept", "title": "2D and 3D shapes"}, {"id": "88318ffc-5c76-4b96-ac2a-a3024e139da0", "type": "concept", "title": "properties"}, {"id": "ed3549aa-62de-422c-a728-3f48c8b33b05", "type": "concept", "title": "symmetry"}, {"id": "f848817e-d4cd-449b-bedf-71f2511ffa09", "type": "concept", "title": "spatial structuring"}], "description": "Why it matters: Children build geometric reasoning by composing shapes, describing attributes, and visualizing transformations."}, {"id": "c8d583ab-bf8c-4979-952a-21290c6c7f58", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Measurement concepts", "children": [{"id": "de7dfcf7-db0a-49c3-9512-af85d2871378", "type": "concept", "title": "length"}, {"id": "6997a143-e98f-4e95-9974-ffa6af090362", "type": "concept", "title": "area"}, {"id": "a9dbcd98-be0f-411e-95e8-912d0c3b6fcc", "type": "concept", "title": "volume"}, {"id": "69a42140-8332-4956-a809-2c5c60eeb38b", "type": "concept", "title": "time"}, {"id": "148ee02e-9dca-4402-943b-fbed8279e039", "type": "concept", "title": "unit conversion"}], "description": "Why it matters: Measurement requires choosing units, iterating them, estimating, and understanding precision."}, {"id": "467d5613-f002-4ba9-83a9-4f3c59c90cab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data and chance", "children": [{"id": "5c475264-0e26-4430-a88e-8d2fcc6f6bd4", "type": "concept", "title": "surveys"}, {"id": "ce1455fc-7c10-460a-9e17-3dd0501b2018", "type": "concept", "title": "line plots"}, {"id": "1c946768-93b7-4d38-94a6-65f4078fc09d", "type": "concept", "title": "bar graphs"}, {"id": "7f302934-9297-409b-84dd-0049f0cc43d5", "type": "concept", "title": "mean as balance point"}, {"id": "987eb5e1-5741-4c80-9ee4-991ac1bf580d", "type": "concept", "title": "informal probability"}], "description": "Why it matters: Data work develops questioning, representation, variability, and interpretation."}]}, {"id": "931e6d22-f4ec-4ef2-8ace-6b9160df1f5b", "type": "topic", "title": "Algebraic Thinking, Patterns, Functions, and Early Generalization", "description": "Algebra in elementary grades is about noticing structure, expressing generality, and reasoning about relationships. It gives students language for patterns long before formal symbolic algebra.", "children": [{"id": "39265d3c-63c9-4f87-bcbe-3b620108425c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Patterns and structure", "children": [{"id": "16c4a8b2-b3fb-4656-8af8-1da89b99f082", "type": "concept", "title": "repeating patterns"}, {"id": "0ff804d2-00e1-422b-9d39-c0dd30090d9d", "type": "concept", "title": "growing patterns"}, {"id": "9e11a510-7de9-48ae-84fa-073c650a16fe", "type": "concept", "title": "skip counting"}, {"id": "49e6a737-b7bf-441b-9641-9cb93fc2f847", "type": "concept", "title": "recursive thinking"}], "description": "Why it matters: Students learn to identify, extend, describe, and justify patterns using words, tables, drawings, and symbols."}, {"id": "57b64bf4-2252-46b2-a4ca-816cc92265e3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equality and unknowns", "children": [{"id": "537c98a2-c876-40dd-a0a1-2e5ad2bedddd", "type": "concept", "title": "balance model"}, {"id": "9cb77a69-1297-43a2-b1d6-3c3146569582", "type": "concept", "title": "unknown quantities"}, {"id": "593760a4-519d-42c1-a89e-f2f22e180d70", "type": "concept", "title": "true/false equations"}, {"id": "59dd8acd-a4e7-4415-99d1-586202f97fef", "type": "concept", "title": "properties of operations"}], "description": "Why it matters: A relational view of the equal sign helps children solve equations meaningfully."}, {"id": "dc7cad3b-34ad-4b71-94cb-64f95f1b96de", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Functions and generalization", "children": [{"id": "8f09c763-2b8c-4c89-a21f-f52c331d4191", "type": "concept", "title": "input-output tables"}, {"id": "0974a033-5647-4f99-aa62-1ddc90b107a1", "type": "concept", "title": "coordinate grids"}, {"id": "e2fd4ed2-1b39-4fe3-a166-238df8e24846", "type": "concept", "title": "function rules"}, {"id": "83927ec9-6fc7-421a-9798-7d251c11d6fb", "type": "concept", "title": "general statements"}], "description": "Why it matters: Students describe how quantities change together and begin to express rules."}]}, {"id": "0323c74d-f42b-47ae-a808-06d074b92ed0", "type": "topic", "title": "Problem Solving, Mathematical Modeling, and Reasoning", "description": "Problem solving teaches students to make sense of situations, choose strategies, test ideas, and explain why results make sense. Modeling connects classroom math to real contexts and decisions.", "children": [{"id": "c5705e56-d036-4114-9830-f5b10f95f168", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Problem-solving strategies", "children": [{"id": "5573ac60-2116-4490-8f6e-e6f4e7b05192", "type": "concept", "title": "draw a diagram"}, {"id": "c7a75726-3a51-44ad-91f7-cc1197f8cc45", "type": "concept", "title": "make a table"}, {"id": "c04c4aa4-7338-4bd2-a955-1f7ac7d4bf49", "type": "concept", "title": "work backward"}, {"id": "103f70da-8aed-4bb6-8417-8b4faaa31709", "type": "concept", "title": "look for a pattern"}], "description": "Why it matters: Students need a repertoire of strategies and the judgment to choose among them."}, {"id": "cb2dce30-17f9-4d55-8005-299b273b9b54", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mathematical modeling", "children": [{"id": "c5896f54-9c3e-4ebc-a20e-eac132238c53", "type": "concept", "title": "context analysis"}, {"id": "18319272-3bbf-46f1-b790-3ef80d9acab4", "type": "concept", "title": "assumptions"}, {"id": "57a2e565-343e-4ff8-95e0-fc3399102e14", "type": "concept", "title": "representations"}, {"id": "fcbeb707-b44a-48e0-ad9b-d2af7bf5c781", "type": "concept", "title": "reasonableness"}], "description": "Why it matters: Modeling asks students to simplify real situations, make assumptions, compute, interpret, and revise."}, {"id": "e186578d-fe88-4744-bc7f-4c41d0e1ec5d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reasoning and proof readiness", "children": [{"id": "c28f80ba-6949-47f7-8abd-215e4bc65daf", "type": "concept", "title": "conjectures"}, {"id": "c0b8571f-10dc-46d1-9f9f-96fe19e76d1a", "type": "concept", "title": "counterexamples"}, {"id": "f3e051f9-a1e6-4c82-87ca-bd4ddfecd1d4", "type": "concept", "title": "generalization"}, {"id": "cc23877d-486e-45a9-a661-09813a6c0299", "type": "concept", "title": "explanation norms"}], "description": "Why it matters: Elementary students can justify claims when teachers press for evidence and connections."}]}, {"id": "02224f06-82b2-4972-8958-93933cfbd7c5", "type": "topic", "title": "Manipulatives, Visual Models, Representations, and Technology", "description": "Representations make abstract ideas available for discussion and refinement. Teachers learn when and how to use tools so students connect concrete, visual, verbal, symbolic, and digital forms.", "children": [{"id": "a648e065-3873-412e-92ca-e628cc02ac7b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Concrete and visual models", "children": [{"id": "069fe57c-5e10-4728-8c01-ef811ea35f38", "type": "concept", "title": "base-ten blocks"}, {"id": "8b3a4243-dce7-4503-9198-d094a236e511", "type": "concept", "title": "fraction strips"}, {"id": "56c37b04-7b47-4ebd-852b-756c8ababaa2", "type": "concept", "title": "arrays"}, {"id": "d14e6f24-a177-4389-a3a8-edd0e5d300c6", "type": "concept", "title": "area models"}], "description": "Why it matters: Manipulatives are most effective when connected explicitly to mathematical ideas and student language."}, {"id": "b2a0c54f-3685-48fa-971d-a2ef4f78682f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Multiple representations", "children": [{"id": "8e80d952-ceeb-479c-9e30-944404185e11", "type": "concept", "title": "CRA sequence"}, {"id": "da626c49-7191-4937-8c8c-4eb83980276b", "type": "concept", "title": "number lines"}, {"id": "fcf2eaa5-274c-4245-bc88-b2a43c0ecb70", "type": "concept", "title": "bar models"}, {"id": "58b0b64e-d5fd-4a04-bc32-10e8acd91072", "type": "concept", "title": "representation matching"}], "description": "Why it matters: Students deepen understanding by translating among drawings, equations, words, tables, and graphs."}, {"id": "3db08543-d07d-4f12-ace0-474a07810c9d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital tools", "children": [{"id": "e067e8a3-3131-426a-959a-55c16a383892", "type": "concept", "title": "virtual manipulatives"}, {"id": "745ee8e8-c723-4fd5-ac87-6a1e4690173a", "type": "concept", "title": "Desmos Classroom"}, {"id": "4db28a6e-f9e9-4691-bddc-3af3a4982800", "type": "concept", "title": "Math Learning Center apps"}, {"id": "fc3b607a-c138-490e-a52a-75b68e1581fb", "type": "concept", "title": "screen-reader considerations"}], "description": "Why it matters: Technology supports exploration, feedback, and accessibility when used for mathematical thinking rather than passive display."}]}, {"id": "777f7529-08ee-4d25-94a2-ef5553a7f18a", "type": "topic", "title": "Math Discourse, Number Talks, Argumentation, and Academic Language", "description": "Mathematical discourse turns student thinking into shared classroom knowledge. Teachers learn to elicit strategies, sequence contributions, support language development, and build norms for critique.", "children": [{"id": "e20d675a-5199-4663-95b3-c18fc984bc86", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Number talks", "children": [{"id": "7c12f697-8579-4e39-9487-f652edb3453a", "type": "concept", "title": "purposeful problems"}, {"id": "c025339c-014a-4456-8e66-435e63dbd037", "type": "concept", "title": "wait time"}, {"id": "852f4a48-8ab3-4583-a916-a9127da88622", "type": "concept", "title": "strategy recording"}, {"id": "aa575231-24a7-4b6a-8784-56de7bc3a419", "type": "concept", "title": "connections among methods"}], "description": "Why it matters: Short mental-math discussions reveal strategies and build flexibility, confidence, and precision."}, {"id": "b287b253-5385-4dd9-bbed-f49c8f6862d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Discussion orchestration", "children": [{"id": "ac167fb9-5474-4356-8f97-2fb338fc70c1", "type": "concept", "title": "5 Practices"}, {"id": "9cfd577f-ba32-46bb-b111-dc24ce6025e8", "type": "concept", "title": "talk moves"}, {"id": "b9b5d8ca-bb63-4047-bbc4-789b77dfd0a8", "type": "concept", "title": "student-to-student response"}, {"id": "a661e3a6-b8ea-4f5e-aa8e-116c2b2c003c", "type": "concept", "title": "summary statements"}], "description": "Why it matters: Teachers select and sequence student ideas so discussions have a mathematical point."}, {"id": "08c08fee-b14a-4e4e-a763-9e63dcae8cee", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Academic language", "children": [{"id": "f0fefc10-4ec0-464c-bb04-7701be478462", "type": "concept", "title": "language objectives"}, {"id": "264c1f2e-ca49-4991-bbb1-d794cefe4403", "type": "concept", "title": "sentence frames"}, {"id": "d0136bfd-0a39-4a12-9e17-5ba0ebc302eb", "type": "concept", "title": "multilingual resources"}, {"id": "092a0245-7bb1-4e55-b43c-fba9b452d211", "type": "concept", "title": "precision without gatekeeping"}], "description": "Why it matters: Students need support using mathematical vocabulary, sentence structures, and representations to explain ideas."}]}, {"id": "e380e7a3-e6ee-485f-aca1-b026fce81b9c", "type": "topic", "title": "Assessment in Elementary Mathematics and Responsive Instruction", "description": "Assessment is a teaching engine, not only a grading event. Teachers learn to gather evidence of thinking, interpret misconceptions, and respond with next instructional moves.", "children": [{"id": "c5010e73-6f00-4655-870e-71dd0ec1276a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Formative assessment", "children": [{"id": "118819c7-64e3-4ccc-a376-813c044230ed", "type": "concept", "title": "exit tickets"}, {"id": "5f7938db-724b-4324-a671-fdad2ca1d14d", "type": "concept", "title": "hinge questions"}, {"id": "9770254c-c412-4a32-8b40-d3397b6ccf81", "type": "concept", "title": "interviews"}, {"id": "46535cae-ff56-4298-953b-da92a0e3b107", "type": "concept", "title": "student work analysis"}], "description": "Why it matters: Quick evidence during learning helps teachers adjust tasks, questions, groups, and supports."}, {"id": "5912e281-b7fe-481a-954f-6911163a2f3f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Performance and portfolio assessment", "children": [{"id": "6de9106f-26f5-4f9b-aa81-89a9dbedd8af", "type": "concept", "title": "rubrics"}, {"id": "44450edc-0fc7-4bf6-8927-e8f043f1d72c", "type": "concept", "title": "criteria"}, {"id": "2166e441-5e9c-41a8-98a5-f0e20145533b", "type": "concept", "title": "portfolio artifacts"}, {"id": "c9d28389-fac3-46a2-be65-fb06216bff2c", "type": "concept", "title": "conferencing"}], "description": "Why it matters: Rich tasks show reasoning, representation, communication, and transfer more fully than isolated items."}, {"id": "04e5f4a9-2ae8-4201-a1ab-cb34a864fb1c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Misconception analysis", "children": [{"id": "c02f5f5e-7df9-408d-9335-e69032855f0f", "type": "concept", "title": "place-value errors"}, {"id": "3b17df4a-218d-4d1f-9513-9a42a63f8a86", "type": "concept", "title": "operation overgeneralization"}, {"id": "df3c71cb-e276-4463-af2d-f79853af8111", "type": "concept", "title": "fraction magnitude"}, {"id": "fa56237b-0aa0-471d-917c-1768a7eca426", "type": "concept", "title": "equal-sign misconceptions"}], "description": "Why it matters: Common errors often reveal sensible but incomplete reasoning, which teachers can build on."}]}, {"id": "1ce2d15e-a773-47ab-b6b0-d50d1b550367", "type": "topic", "title": "Equity, Culturally Responsive Math Teaching, and Math Anxiety", "description": "Elementary math teaching treats equity as part of mathematical quality. This topic focuses on access, representation, identity, and classroom conditions that reduce anxiety and expand participation.", "children": [{"id": "b5fc3e07-9cfc-4f9b-a79b-b4e0ab16e691", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equitable participation", "children": [{"id": "8fb86a6a-f89e-4308-b57b-15ed2e4fa08e", "type": "concept", "title": "status patterns"}, {"id": "dce0a2e0-4628-42bc-a9d3-ba18374c5685", "type": "concept", "title": "group roles"}, {"id": "2d868fbd-9ba9-417a-be8b-19bf55906b5f", "type": "concept", "title": "participation structures"}, {"id": "19754865-9e3d-400b-b857-9c8c6eb6db60", "type": "concept", "title": "teacher noticing"}], "description": "Why it matters: Teachers design routines that distribute authority, visibility, and intellectual responsibility across students."}, {"id": "43ffca97-4ace-4e01-837e-fcee19734e85", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Culturally responsive tasks", "children": [{"id": "afddf14e-5169-4316-9801-3057e5c0aab7", "type": "concept", "title": "community data"}, {"id": "eb48391b-a865-4f3d-8808-48e3273a0266", "type": "concept", "title": "funds of knowledge"}, {"id": "c1af5ffb-903c-4797-88bf-8727ef191109", "type": "concept", "title": "choice"}, {"id": "58caeef3-10eb-467c-81b0-d64019822c41", "type": "concept", "title": "critical numeracy"}], "description": "Why it matters: Context-rich mathematics can connect to students' lives while maintaining rigor and avoiding stereotypes."}, {"id": "6618bf37-5fbc-4df0-accb-0e9926e4b8b7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Math anxiety and belonging", "children": [{"id": "6390e2dd-af54-4926-b248-a44d9d8c8771", "type": "concept", "title": "low-floor high-ceiling tasks"}, {"id": "c24b1f6b-3054-4e7e-ac2e-bb9ea1388067", "type": "concept", "title": "error analysis"}, {"id": "4e3c18dc-4fe8-49bf-8c81-37141bedef4f", "type": "concept", "title": "feedback language"}, {"id": "927e6eec-276d-4f45-8da0-2f0c24fd2499", "type": "concept", "title": "family messages"}], "description": "Why it matters: Reducing anxiety requires predictable routines, strategy validation, and assessment practices that value growth."}]}, {"id": "0a952519-9425-484d-be78-d1f0f33badf5", "type": "topic", "title": "Differentiation, UDL, MTSS, and Inclusive Math Instruction", "description": "Inclusive math instruction anticipates learner variability and provides multiple pathways into rigorous ideas. Teachers learn to support students with disabilities, multilingual learners, and advanced learners without lowering expectations.", "children": [{"id": "010979d9-9f66-45f0-b4d1-8bf60f4c0263", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Universal Design for Learning", "children": [{"id": "5de2ef54-b912-4f01-9f3e-69267403b685", "type": "concept", "title": "choice"}, {"id": "a79e8db3-3e0e-4529-953d-6327d93d155a", "type": "concept", "title": "visual supports"}, {"id": "26363b01-9b88-4fc4-a7ec-d00506054db0", "type": "concept", "title": "accessible materials"}, {"id": "707611e6-3d02-4962-99ea-a7be1794b0a6", "type": "concept", "title": "executive-function scaffolds"}], "description": "Why it matters: UDL helps teachers plan multiple means of engagement, representation, and expression from the start."}, {"id": "7d635c38-a753-48fd-a0cf-28eb746e952c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "MTSS and intervention", "children": [{"id": "8ea7908a-7a81-4df4-94ce-278ff83d31cf", "type": "concept", "title": "screening"}, {"id": "af9e9a47-a0ed-4918-a4eb-6a7fe49c6536", "type": "concept", "title": "progress monitoring"}, {"id": "e31652b7-17ff-4342-bbb6-c83379d4ab81", "type": "concept", "title": "small-group lessons"}, {"id": "c17eaf10-dc0c-4e4c-bde0-35e5c3a0a89d", "type": "concept", "title": "intervention cycles"}], "description": "Why it matters: Tiered supports use evidence to identify needs and intensify instruction while keeping students connected to grade-level ideas."}, {"id": "727eda99-14b2-4f4b-987a-78a24bf38d16", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Specially designed math instruction", "children": [{"id": "1002fe04-06ac-41ee-91c1-6c5a6ffe7884", "type": "concept", "title": "IEP alignment"}, {"id": "5638a314-2a31-4502-9a3e-46a6e2ce13ef", "type": "concept", "title": "accommodations"}, {"id": "2bc8a0fe-db9d-4162-8f98-0cba91979f72", "type": "concept", "title": "assistive technology"}, {"id": "6dbf8e0d-fa39-4348-b07c-102e0fc3eb11", "type": "concept", "title": "co-teaching"}], "description": "Why it matters: Teachers adapt tasks, language, materials, and assessment while preserving the mathematical target."}]}, {"id": "fafc10b6-080a-40d0-9494-341ebf2bcf4e", "type": "topic", "title": "Lesson Design, Task Selection, and Classroom Implementation", "description": "This topic turns theory into teachable lessons. Teachers learn to select worthwhile tasks, anticipate student thinking, launch clearly, facilitate productively, and close with mathematical clarity.", "children": [{"id": "cf3d5034-09f2-4405-907d-f75d8c467752", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Task selection and adaptation", "children": [{"id": "3dc3d7f3-f53b-47fd-83c5-a8f01204feef", "type": "concept", "title": "cognitive demand"}, {"id": "98b28322-6728-44f7-847c-714ab6f8c3a6", "type": "concept", "title": "low-floor high-ceiling"}, {"id": "acef7df3-27b9-470a-925c-d52a2bd23c8f", "type": "concept", "title": "context adaptation"}, {"id": "091d5b2d-a532-464e-9886-805af2aa9ee7", "type": "concept", "title": "extension questions"}], "description": "Why it matters: A strong task invites reasoning, multiple strategies, and visible evidence of the learning goal."}, {"id": "84e910db-b1f2-4604-a985-8a46e56ee5c9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lesson architecture", "children": [{"id": "37a75cf8-1dbd-47e0-8874-e0741a5b7c98", "type": "concept", "title": "launch"}, {"id": "8fc218ba-bd17-48ff-903e-8ce0fd5b2d27", "type": "concept", "title": "monitoring"}, {"id": "599229e1-82c3-4f4b-9dd7-87a244dbc0e8", "type": "concept", "title": "selecting and sequencing"}, {"id": "5d676327-3b40-4e23-b3f7-f9019482aa0a", "type": "concept", "title": "closure"}], "description": "Why it matters: Effective lessons have a clear arc from launch to exploration to discussion to consolidation."}, {"id": "2ea4cf0d-a915-4087-a012-3962613d99d7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Classroom implementation", "children": [{"id": "c127c0a3-d508-48d3-be58-9452c10dec98", "type": "concept", "title": "routines"}, {"id": "9ce245f8-7eca-4e67-87fe-d260defc8424", "type": "concept", "title": "grouping"}, {"id": "b107a7cd-780f-4314-8b99-340fcb9ce7f6", "type": "concept", "title": "teacher questioning"}, {"id": "ef73daf6-e76e-4345-b05a-91dabd0dd3ec", "type": "concept", "title": "transitions"}], "description": "Why it matters: Teachers manage materials, time, groups, and behavior so cognitive work stays central."}]}, {"id": "151fe1e7-a40f-43c1-b2bd-9821f2ab7a82", "type": "topic", "title": "Practicum: Elementary Math Teaching Portfolio", "description": "The practicum strand asks teacher candidates to document growth through planning, teaching, assessment, reflection, and revision. The portfolio makes professional judgment visible.", "children": [{"id": "7582dda6-415a-4594-ba32-7a90f7cb45ec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Teaching demonstrations", "children": [{"id": "9282a95f-9fb1-4912-9886-647fae39d864", "type": "concept", "title": "microteaching"}, {"id": "8bbc7818-87c4-480f-bd22-9a1643da20f5", "type": "concept", "title": "video reflection"}, {"id": "d5594d6c-6119-4801-887c-c683033409a8", "type": "concept", "title": "peer feedback"}, {"id": "2770d93d-6e2d-4908-8cd1-69c97939739c", "type": "concept", "title": "mentor observation"}], "description": "Why it matters: Candidates practice teaching short math lessons and use feedback to improve clarity, questioning, and responsiveness."}, {"id": "85743ab9-1d12-4afb-85fa-5637015f1f40", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Student work study", "children": [{"id": "2ee48ef2-efa8-424c-ad58-1e211a295188", "type": "concept", "title": "error patterns"}, {"id": "4b3f9e89-72c8-4dc1-8a49-284de8fce89d", "type": "concept", "title": "strategy diversity"}, {"id": "d6c0b563-a0c5-4a70-8cae-54ed5a64cd38", "type": "concept", "title": "rubric calibration"}, {"id": "e036611b-3d45-4baa-9b85-714f477dbf3e", "type": "concept", "title": "responsive re-teaching"}], "description": "Why it matters: Analyzing authentic student work develops noticing and helps teachers plan next steps."}, {"id": "c04429a0-5ecd-455b-9562-ca842618de13", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional portfolio", "children": [{"id": "866845ff-6b86-4d7b-95f4-96d26ef9790d", "type": "concept", "title": "lesson plans"}, {"id": "f965a284-6511-422e-adc3-a817e563d652", "type": "concept", "title": "assessment artifacts"}, {"id": "f8f85d70-76c6-4cf3-bb2a-241504b51ea5", "type": "concept", "title": "reflection memos"}, {"id": "a2b7fc05-4ac3-4414-979f-46ccf5c7c445", "type": "concept", "title": "equity commitments"}], "description": "Why it matters: A portfolio gathers evidence that the candidate can design, enact, assess, and reflect on elementary math instruction."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$temajson$::jsonb,
